<p>In the latest escalation, President Trump gave Iran 48 hours to fully reopen the Strait of Hormuz or face US strikes on Iranian power plants. Iranian officials and the Revolutionary Guards said Tehran would answer by targeting power stations supplying US bases and, in some reports, broader Gulf energy and water infrastructure. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu also said Israel would back US strikes if Iran did not reopen the waterway. The confrontation comes in the fourth week of the US-Israel-Iran war, with the strait largely disrupted since February 28 and concerns growing over oil supply, shipping, and regional stability. Multiple reports say Tehran has threatened to close the strait completely if the US attacks its electricity infrastructure, raising the risk that a conflict already centered on missile and military exchanges could spread to civilian systems relied on by millions across the Gulf.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/dWOZyeoQvAJOUzhnyslFl-Eo2V70ljf0xoHJB6OLdwECgXmJ4YmuJueL6OW5Pr18ZgRBrlSRk6El6o-dM5DFKdggnsXwzUTQ2CNeDU7PlFzofu0BZ7-FHdiv_QAmrZTnz9VBJiE2ZISIyJt1lNk2dxt5b7pOPDSvOU0ySBRuNKY-RCkHc5MF0XpPBGgbJeSwm3mIsPtkCDNJUYIdkS_tVD9NO9curZ3Suuc' alt='Tehran residents on Sunday, as tensions rose over possible power cuts affecting the capital.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Civilian risk: Reuters-based coverage said Iranian threats initially included desalination plants, which are crucial for drinking water in Gulf states, though a later statement appeared to narrow the warning to power plants linked to Israel and US bases.</li><li>War toll: Iran’s Health Ministry said US-Israeli attacks since February 28 have killed at least 1,444 people and injured 18,551, while retaliatory Iranian strikes killed 15 people in Israel and seven US service members at regional bases, according to RT’s roundup.</li><li>Market alarm: International Energy Agency chief Fatih Birol warned the Hormuz crisis could cause a bigger shock than the oil crises of the 1970s, as energy prices kept rising and analysts described markets as highly uncertain.</li><li>Lebanon front: As the Hormuz standoff intensified, Israel signaled plans to expand ground operations against Hezbollah in southern Lebanon and said it had destroyed bridges across the Litani River.</li></ul><blockquote>Do not doubt that we will do this. - Iranian Revolutionary Guard statement read on state television</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He set a two-day deadline for Iran to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and threatened to &quot;obliterate&quot; Iranian power plants if Tehran did not comply. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-israel-gas-and-oil-prices-trump-netanyahu-strait-hormuz/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Iranian Revolutionary Guards: The Guards said Iran would retaliate for any strike on its electricity sector by targeting Israeli power plants and plants supplying US bases in regional countries. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-points-tit-tat-retaliation-if-power-plants-targeted-statement'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Benjamin Netanyahu: The Israeli prime minister said Israel would back US strikes on Iran’s power grid if Tehran refused to reopen the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/22/we-do-it-together-in-confidence-netanyahu-backs-us-strikes-on-iran'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Iranian civilians: The New York Times reported that some war-weary Iranians were panicking at the prospect of strikes on power plants and feared another sharp decline in daily life. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/22/world/middleeast/iran-trump-power-plants.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>International Energy Agency: IEA head Fatih Birol warned that the crisis around the strait poses a major threat to the world economy because of the strait’s central role in oil flows. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-world-economy-facing-major-threat-iea-head-says/live-76478747'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/shorts/nVMVLNb_Gbs'>Strait of Hormuz: Trump’s ultimatum to Iran • FRANCE 24 English</a> - youtube.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635868-iran-war-fourth-week/'>Iran vows to target neighbors’ water and energy infrastructure if US strikes power plants</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-israel-iran-war-iran-missile-strike-on-israel-iran-targets-israeli-nuclear-facility-dimona-arad-trump-warns-iran-strait-of-hormuz-diego-garcia-11249333#publisher=newsstand'>US-Israel-Iran War Updates: Ahead Of Trump’s Deadline, Iran Warns It May Target Regional Power Infrastructure</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-israel-gas-and-oil-prices-trump-netanyahu-strait-hormuz/'>Iran says Strait of Hormuz will be &quot;completely closed&quot; if Trump delivers on threats</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-trump-threatens-to-escalate-iran-attacks-after-suggesting-war-winding/'>Trump threatens to escalate Iran attacks after suggesting war &#x27;winding down&#x27;</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-22-0700/foreign-policy-iran-says-strait-hormuz-will-be-completely-closed-if-trump-delivers-threat-strike-power-plants'>Iran says Strait of Hormuz will be &#x27;completely closed&#x27; if Trump delivers on threat to strike power plants</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/23/iran-threatens-to-attack-us-bases-power-plants-as-trumps-deadline-on-strait-of-hormuz-appr'>Iran vows to strike US bases&#x27; power plants as Trump&#x27;s deadline on Strait of Hormuz nears</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-points-tit-tat-retaliation-if-power-plants-targeted-statement'>Iran points at tit for tat retaliation if power plants targeted, statement</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a